      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of \"necessary friction\" is a pragmatic acknowledgment that economic progress requires adaptation, not a dismissal of human suffering. Governments are not solely responsible for micro-managing every industry; their role is to create the stable, predictable environment that allows global trade to flourish. When nations prioritize protectionism over global integration, they risk economic stagnation and isolation, ultimately harming their own citizens' long-term prosperity.",
      "source": "target",
